  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41301" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Framework for the Progressive Control of Transboundary Animal Diseases (GF-TADs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support global, regional, and national actions required to control and subsequently eradicate transboundary diseases, including FMD, ASF and PPR with high threat impact potential across DTRA BTRP partner regions. The efforts will ultimately aim to control and develop action plans for the control of TADs of security concern. The provided
leadership and expertise will help to improve coordination among key members within animal health sectors at the global, regional, and national levels. The impact of this work will be a reduction of the threat posed by emerging, transboundary, and endemic pathogens of security concern through development of disease risk mitigation strategies, enhancing awareness of disease, and developing methods to better identify disease presence and risk. Outcomes of this
work will result in enhanced capabilities for early detection, response and control of high security pathogens.</narrative>
  </description>
